# Result summary
Question: in which years is wealth of individuals with a criminal record (ever_jailed==1)
significantly LOWER than without? Years tested: 1985, 1990, 1996. Primary = all 12,013 rows.

Primary test: one-sided tie-corrected Mann-Whitney U, alpha=0.05, Holm across the 3 years.
VERDICT: 1985 PASS, 1990 PASS, 1996 PASS (all three years; every criterion).
Interpretation split: 1985 = pre-/concurrent-exposure gap (selection); 1990 & 1996 = post-exposure.

Key numbers (primary):
 1985 n=289/11,724 medians 720 vs 3,600  HL=-1,260 [-2,100,-500] delta=-0.218 MWU p=8.0e-11 Holm 8.0e-11
 1990 n=289/11,724 medians 0 vs 10,500   HL=-7,850 [-10,300,-5,400] delta=-0.420 MWU p=3.9e-35 Holm 1.2e-34
 1996 n=289/11,724 medians 0 vs 8,500    HL=-6,000 [-10,200,-3,000] delta=-0.351 MWU p=4.6e-26 Holm 9.3e-26
 P(wealth>0) RR = 0.807 / 0.611 / 0.621 (1985/1990/1996), Fisher p = 2.5e-06 / 7.0e-22 / 1.9e-14
 Gap ratio (jailed mean / non-jailed mean) = 0.316 -> 0.221 -> 0.193 : the gap WIDENS post-exposure.

Audits requested:
 * Tie correction: term=229/183/658 (1.9%/1.5%/5.5% variance reduction); corrected p is 1.5x/3.2x/20.9x
   SMALLER than uncorrected; 1996 verdict unchanged (both << 0.05/3). Tie correction cannot flip PASS->FAIL.
 * Permutation null (20,000): p_perm = 1/20001 = 5.0e-5 (floor) all years -> asymptotic p corroborated.
 * Implementation validated: my tie-corrected p matches scipy.mannwhitneyu to ~4 decimal digits of mantissa.
 * Negative control (300 label permutations): rejection rate 0.057/0.043/0.033 vs nominal 0.05 -> calibrated.
 * CI DISAGREEMENT (surfaced, not hidden): crude normal-approx HL interval based on the pooled SD spans
   zero (e.g. 1996 [-36,661, +24,661]) while bootstrap [-8,000,-4,100] and Hollander-Wolfe [-10,200,-3,000]
   exclude it. The crude interval is INVALID for a rank-shift statistic under skew 6-17/kurtosis 46-372;
   the two legitimate (rank-based / bootstrap) intervals agree with each other.
Sensitivities: dedup (12,013->10,114 rows) -> all 3 PASS, effects LARGER (delta -0.275/-0.511/-0.424);
 winsor@p99 -> all 3 PASS (rank tests are order-invariant; only Welch moved, and it got MORE significant);
 race x sex (18 cells) -> every cell negative in direction; 5/6, 6/6, 6/6 cells Holm-significant per year;
 2 cells (black|male 1990, hipanic|male 1996) fail ONLY the Welch criterion due to extreme right-tail
 leverage in small jailed cells -> documented weakness of criterion c3.
